  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "∀ x : ℝ, Filter.Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (1 + x / ↑n) ^ n) Filter.atTop (nhds (Real.exp x))",
    "plain": "Prove the classical limit definition of the exponential function: lim_{n→∞} (1 + x/n)^n = e^x, from first principles using the derivative of log at 1.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "One of the most fundamental limits in analysis",
      "Not available in Mathlib v4.26.0 — fills a genuine gap",
      "Foundation for Poisson limit theorem, continuous compounding, and Euler's number"
    ]
  },
